From 638776fd4deca496df1fc012ae09d08b5996c607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:34:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] recursion: child-meta mode of the verifier sub-circuit
 (T7c)

VerifierConfig::child_meta = Some(h): the per-AIR constants of the child
key that ProofShapeAir took as constraints are rows of the cached
constraint-DAG trace instead (fixed height h), sent on a meta bus by
SymbolicExpressionAir and received by ProofShapeAir. The verifier
key then depends only on the child parameter set, so one L key verifies
N3 (full tree) and the path C leaf layer; the cached commitment X tells
the children apart. Default None keeps every existing key unchanged.
